      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T17:18:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In terms of API design, adding a new flag making the \"`full`\" debug mode even _fuller_ is confusing, IMO. Could this functionality be added under `--debug full`, without CLI change?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "8c4e156ea2fdc73d774528e92742ac4cc3ae0929",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "71d16d5d_e8faf67a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T10:49:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Overall the policy in Android is to keep debuggable builds as close as possible to non-debuggable. I think when possible we should adhere to the same policy for VMs.\n\nAdditionally, in most cases we don\u0027t really care about earlycon, so it would just spam logs of debuggable VMs. If we find ourselves to always use --enable-earlycon flag, then we can either incorporate it into --debug full, or make it true by default.",
      "parentUuid": "40da2df0_660fea41",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "8c4e156ea2fdc73d774528e92742ac4cc3ae0929",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01e570e0_89795769",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T13:46:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack that we don\u0027t want `earlycon` to be enabled by default.\n\nThe `vm` CLI has already caused confusion in the past and I don\u0027t believe that adding yet another flag is improving its clarity. As you show in `Test:`, you felt the need to test `--enable-earlycon` with `--debug none` but ideally, it shouldn\u0027t even be possible to express that combo. The need for this assertion is another symptom\n\n    if config.debug.enable_earlycon() {\n        if config.debug.debug !\u003d DebugLevel::FULL {\n            bail!(\"earlycon is only supported for debuggable VMs\")\n        }\n\nIMO, extending `--debug` (e.g. comma separated list of \"features\") might have made more sense but anyway, I\u0027ll +2 as this isn\u0027t _super_ important and is likely not the best use of our time.",
      "parentUuid": "71d16d5d_e8faf67a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "8c4e156ea2fdc73d774528e92742ac4cc3ae0929",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
